# Infrastructure and Operations

- Local development must work without AWS. Promote the same immutable application images through staging and production.
- Containers run non-root, have health checks, bounded resources, read-only filesystems where practical, and no embedded secrets.
- Parser/OCR execution has no network or application secrets, uses a constrained sandbox, and preserves the shared-kernel risk/upgrade ADR.
- Production API traffic passes through CloudFront/WAF and hardened Caddy; EC2 origin, private ParadeDB, both Valkey instances, and egress proxies are not publicly reachable.
- Pin ParadeDB image digest and `pg_search`/schema/index versions. Use separate bootstrap/writer/read-only credentials, an encrypted working volume, no browser/provider egress, explicit CPU/memory/statement limits, health/lag/rebuild alarms, and the signed Community/Enterprise plus same-host TLS/availability ADR.
- Split Valkey rate/cache instances, disable `nopass`, use named ACL users, explicit memory/eviction policies, and hard container limits. Test auth-limit fallback/fail-closed behavior when limits Valkey is unavailable; omitting TLS on same-host isolated networks requires the plan's explicit ADR and credential-rotation controls.
- Deny direct container egress: API/agents use provider allowlists, only the crawl proxy reaches public web destinations, and ParadeDB/parser/OCR have no route.
- Preserve SSE flushing, 15-second heartbeats, explicit 90-second Caddy/CloudFront origin read and keep-alive timeouts, event resume, and connection limits; stage-test a 50-second run.
- Managed deployments use GitHub OIDC and protected production environments. Migration credentials stay in Secrets Manager and are fetched by the one-shot SSM job, never stored in GitHub.
- Workstation AWS for this repo uses local profile `Nagdy-iam` (IAM user `Muna`, account `665602132723`, region `us-east-1`). Credentials live only in `%USERPROFILE%\\.aws\\credentials`. Never commit keys, paste them into chat, put them in `.env`, or copy them onto EC2. Unset `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` and set `AWS_PROFILE=Nagdy-iam` plus `AWS_EC2_METADATA_DISABLED=true`. Do not use `aws login` or `export-credentials` for this workstation unless `Nagdy-iam` is missing.
- Deploy health-gated blue/green API slots on EC2. Keep the old slot active until the new slot is ready; support immutable rollback.
- Treat Supabase as durable authority. Treat Valkey as ephemeral and ParadeDB as a derived projection that must rebuild from reconciled Supabase state; an EBS snapshot may accelerate but never replace that path. Verify backup, restore, clean BM25 rebuild/parity, instance rebuild, and RTO/RPO.
- Staging must exercise managed Supabase pooling, private ParadeDB projection/recheck/outage/rebuild, asymmetric JWKS rollover, Auth/SES, Storage, CloudFront/WAF, origin-secret dual rotation, egress, audit-chain mutation and KMS/S3 Object Lock anchors/export, alert routing, Vercel, restore, and rollback before production.
- CI has no failure-swallowing commands and runs the test tiers defined in the plan.

## Change proof

- Validate Compose/IaC, build and scan images, test health/readiness including ParadeDB projection lag/version/fallback, and document ports, canonical-versus-derived state, credentials, rebuild/rollback, and monitoring impact.
